cookbook/references/kaggriculture-configs-follow-isaiahs-scaling-6m-recipe.md:25:  - `check_workload_headroom` divides these by the model's own `rows_per_chunk` (709 padded tokens × width 512, giving 5,915 rows) and `head_rows_per_chunk` (11,096). It raises when one row cannot fit either limit or a workload is empty. Head calls are exact. Trunk figures assume full padding, so trunk calls are an **upper bound** and trunk headroom a **lower bound**: the packed path plans chunks from actual token counts (16,384 rows of 300 tokens need 2 packed chunks, not 3).
